#: ../../../installation.rst:5
msgid "Installing Poe the Poet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:7
msgid ""
"There are a few ways to install Poe the Poet depending on your preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:10
msgid "1. Install the CLI globally *(recommended)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:12
msgid ""
"The following methods will make the ``poe`` executable available anywhere on "
"your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:15
msgid "With |pipx_link|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:235
msgid "<a href=\"https://pypa.github.io/pipx/\" target=\"_blank\">pipx</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:17
msgid "pipx install poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:23
msgid "With |uv_link|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:239
msgid "<a href=\"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/\" target=\"_blank\">uv</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:25
msgid "uv tool install poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:30
msgid "With |brew_link|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:243
msgid "<a href=\"https://brew.sh/\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:32
msgid ""
"brew tap nat-n/poethepoet\n"
"brew install nat-n/poethepoet/poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:37
msgid "See the |formula_link|."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:247
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://github.com/nat-n/homebrew-poethepoet\" "
"target=\"_blank\">homebrew formula</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:40
msgid "With pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:42
msgid ""
"Of course you can also install it with pip – assuming your current python "
"environment is global."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:44
msgid "pip install poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:49
msgid "2. Install poethepoet as a :doc:`poetry plugin<poetry_plugin>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:51
msgid "You can install the poethepoet poetry plugin globally like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:53
msgid "poetry self add 'poethepoet[poetry_plugin]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:57
msgid ""
"Or add it to poetry on a per project basis by adding the following to your "
"*pyproject.toml*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:59
msgid ""
"[tool.poetry.requires-plugins]\n"
"poethepoet = { version = \"~0.35.0\", extras = [\"poetry_plugin\"]}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:64
msgid ""
"See the |poetry_plugin_link| for more installation options, or see the :doc:"
"`poetry plugin docs <poetry_plugin>` for more details about this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:251
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://python-poetry.org/docs/main/plugins/#using-plugins\" "
"target=\"_blank\">poetry docs</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:68
msgid "3. Install poethepoet into your project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:71
msgid "With poetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:73 ../../../installation.rst:86
msgid "Add poethepoet as a dev dependency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:73
msgid "poetry add --group dev poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:78 ../../../installation.rst:91
msgid "And run it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:78
msgid "poetry run poe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:84
msgid "With uv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:86
msgid "uv add --dev poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:91
msgid "uv run poe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:99
msgid "Enable tab completion for your shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:101
msgid ""
"Poe comes with tab completion scripts for bash, zsh, and fish to save you "
"keystrokes. How to install them will depend on your shell setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:106
msgid ""
"We believe installing the poe CLI globally offers the best developer "
"experience. However if for some reason you prefer *not* to then you can "
"still benefit from shell completions if you create an appropriate alias in "
"your shell, such as one of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:108
msgid ":sh:`alias poe=\"poetry run poe\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:109
msgid ":sh:`alias poe=\"poetry poe\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:110
msgid ":sh:`alias poe=\"uv run poe\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:113
msgid "Zsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:115
msgid ""
"# oh-my-zsh\n"
"mkdir -p ~/.oh-my-zsh/completions\n"
"poe _zsh_completion > ~/.oh-my-zsh/completions/_poe\n"
"\n"
"# without oh-my-zsh\n"
"mkdir -p ~/.zfunc/\n"
"poe _zsh_completion > ~/.zfunc/_poe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:125
msgid "Zsh completion includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:127 ../../../installation.rst:159
#: ../../../installation.rst:189
msgid "Global CLI options (``-v``, ``-C``, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:128
msgid "Task names with help text descriptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:129
msgid "Task-specific arguments (options and positional args)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:133
msgid ""
"You'll need to start a new shell for the new completion script to be loaded. "
"If it still doesn't work try adding a call to :sh:`compinit` to the end of "
"your zshrc file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:135
msgid ""
"In some cases when upgrading to a newer version of the completion script it "
"may be necessary to clean the zsh completions cache with `rm ~/.zcompdump*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:138
msgid "Bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:140
msgid ""
"# Quick setup - add to ~/.bashrc\n"
"eval \"$(poe _bash_completion)\"\n"
"\n"
"# Or install to a file (requires new shell to take effect):\n"
"\n"
"# User local (recommended)\n"
"mkdir -p ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions\n"
"poe _bash_completion > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/poe\n"
"\n"
"# System-wide\n"
"poe _bash_completion | sudo tee /etc/bash_completion.d/poe > /dev/null\n"
"\n"
"# Homebrew bash\n"
"poe _bash_completion > $(brew --prefix)/etc/bash_completion.d/poe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:157
msgid "Bash completion includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:160 ../../../installation.rst:190
msgid "Task names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:161 ../../../installation.rst:191
msgid "Task-specific arguments and choices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:165
msgid ""
"If completions don't work after installing to a file, ensure you have the "
"``bash-completion`` package installed and that it's sourced in your ``~/."
"bashrc``. You may need to start a new shell session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:168
msgid "Fish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:170
msgid ""
"# Fish\n"
"poe _fish_completion > ~/.config/fish/completions/poe.fish\n"
"\n"
"# Homebrew fish\n"
"poe _fish_completion > (brew --prefix)/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/poe."
"fish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:179
msgid "Powershell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:181
msgid ""
"# add to $PROFILE\n"
"poe _powershell_completion | out-string | invoke-expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:187
msgid "Powershell completion includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:195
msgid ""
"You'll need to start a new shell for the new completion script to be loaded. "
"Alternatively, you can invoke ``. $PROFILE`` to reload your profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:199
msgid "Install the poethepoet AI Agent skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:201
msgid ""
"The official poethepoet skill can help your AI Agent use poethepoet more "
"effectively. It covers discovering and executing tasks, as well as more in-"
"depth guidance on creating them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:204
msgid "Install via the built in ``_install_skill`` task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:206
msgid ""
"Poe ships with a task to install the skill (similar to how shell completions "
"are installed):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:208
msgid ""
"poe _install_skill                         # auto-detects .claude/.codex/."
"pi/.agents and prompts\n"
"poe _install_skill ~/.claude/skills        # explicit path (substitute your "
"agent's dir)\n"
"poe _install_skill <skills-dir> --upgrade  # non-interactive upgrade (skips "
"if same/newer)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:215
msgid "Install from GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:217
msgid ""
"You can also install the skill directly from github, such as by using |"
"vercel_skills_link|:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:255
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://vercel.com/docs/agent-resources/skills\" "
"target=\"_blank\">Vercel Agent Skills</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:219
msgid ""
"npx skills add https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/tree/v0.46.0/poethepoet/"
"skills/poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:225
msgid ""
"The skill is versioned in step with poe. After upgrading poe, re-run the "
"install task with ``--upgrade`` (shown above) to refresh the installed copy "
"— it skips the copy if the installed version is already current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:229
msgid "Supported python versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:231
msgid ""
"Poe the Poet officially supports python >=3.10, and is tested with python "
"3.10 to 3.14 on macOS, linux and windows."
msgstr ""
